"Cadmium": "鎘",
"Plating waste": "電鍍廢棄物",
"A soft, mobile metal. Cd²⁺ binds much less strongly to soil than lead, so more of it stays in solution, especially in acidic soils, and crops such as rice take it up readily.": "柔軟、移動性高的金屬。Cd²⁺ 與土壤的結合遠比鉛弱，較多留在溶液中，酸性土壤尤其明顯，稻米等作物很容易吸收。",
"Keep soil pH near neutral, keep paddies flooded during grain filling where cadmium is the concern, keep polluted water out of irrigation channels, and remove or replace heavily polluted topsoil.": "讓土壤 pH 維持在接近中性；有鎘疑慮的稻田在穀粒充實期保持淹水；不讓污染水進入灌溉渠道；移除或更換嚴重污染的表土。",
"Accumulates in the kidneys over decades and damages them; also weakens bone. Food, especially rice and other grains, is the main route for non-smokers. Tolerable weekly intake 2.5 µg/kg body weight (EFSA 2011).": "在腎臟累積數十年並造成損傷，也會使骨骼變脆弱。對不吸菸者而言，食物（尤其稻米等穀物）是主要暴露途徑。每週容許攝入量 2.5 µg/kg 體重（EFSA 2011）。",
"Taiwan soil pollution control standard for Cd: 20 mg/kg, or 5 mg/kg on food-crop farmland (monitoring standard 10 and 2.5 mg/kg).": "台灣土壤污染管制標準（鎘）：20 mg/kg，食用作物農地 5 mg/kg（監測標準 10 和 2.5 mg/kg）。",
"Taiwan drinking-water standard for Cd: 0.005 mg/L. Groundwater control standard: 0.0050 mg/L (class 1), 0.050 mg/L (class 2).": "台灣飲用水水質標準（鎘）：0.005 mg/L。地下水污染管制標準：0.0050 mg/L（第一類）、0.050 mg/L（第二類）。",
